<title>KENYA: Kenya pipeline fire kills four.</title>
<headline>Kenya pipeline fire kills four.</headline>
<dateline>MOMBASA, Kenya 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four people died and a fifth was severely burned when a leaking gas pipeline caught fire near a refinery at Mombasa, Kenya, witnesses said.</p>
<p>Total Kenya marketing manager Ken Ikiara said the fire started where excavation for a new gas pipeline was being carried out near pipelines carrying liquefied petroleum gas, kerosene and gasoline.</p>
<p>Mombasa firefighters took seven hours to put out the blaze, which destroyed a warehouse full of electronic equipment and damaged a transformer carrying power to around 50,000 people.</p>
